ert and Milo Barbell","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/calvert-and-milo-barbell/283008","site":"T Nation · 837 posts · 2023"}],"news":[],"social":[{"title":"A mystery of the ketogenic diet: benevolent pseudo-diabetes in mice (2019)","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=31755361","site":"Hacker News","score":135,"comments":138,"year":2022},{"title":"Patients say keto helps with mental illness. Science is racing to understand why","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=39186770","site":"Hacker News","score":118,"comments":138,"year":2024},{"title":"Pilot study shows ketogenic diet improves mental illness","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=39900857","site":"Hacker News","score":126,"comments":102,"year":2024},{"title":"Ketogenic Diet Intervention on Metabolic and Psychiatric Health","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=39896423","site":"Hacker News","score":85,"comments":116,"year":2024},{"title":"Ketogenic diet helps tame flu virus in mice","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=21650544","site":"Hacker News","score":111,"comments":63,"year":2019},{"title":"3 huge new studies of 0.5MM people are casting major doubts on the keto diet","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=18039829","site":"Hacker News","score":41,"comments":73,"year":2018},{"title":"Restricted Ketogenic Diet Therapy for Primary Lung Cancer with Brain Metastasis","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=38267020","site":"Hacker News","score":53,"comments":60,"year":2023},{"title":"The ketogenic diet improves healthspan and memory in aging mice","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40812537","site":"Hacker News","score":47,"comments":34,"year":2024},{"title":"Ketogenic Diet Shows Promise Treating Serious Mental Illness in Stanford Study","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=41427648","site":"Hacker News","score":15,"comments":37,"year":2024},{"title":"Can a keto diet reverse diabetes?","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=18685060","site":"Hacker News","score":37,"comments":12,"year":2018},{"title":"Chronic Schizophrenia Put into Remission with Ketogenic Diet","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=20421989","site":"Hacker News","score":33,"comments":14,"year":2019},{"title":"Keto diet works best in small doses, mouse study finds","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=22318914","site":"Hacker News","score":30,"comments":13,"year":2020},{"title":"Ketogenic diet may play a role in treating schizophrenia: research (2019)","url":"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40043711","site":"Hacker News","score":25,"comments":12,"year":2024}],"web":[{"title":"Ketogenic diet","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ketogenic_diet"},{"title":"Low-carbohydrate diet","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Low-carbohydrate_diet"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Fat loss","chain":["Very low carbohydrate intake","Lower appetite, body fat falls","Leaner face and body"],"effect":"indirect","text":"Very low carbohydrate intake lowers appetite and body fat for a leaner face and body, and some users report calmer skin. Keto is an established epilepsy therapy with mixed weight loss results; acne effects were not covered in the sources here."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["The ketogenic diet is a high-fat, adequate-protein, very low-carbohydrate diet in which the liver produces ketone bodies as fuel. It was developed as a medical therapy for refractory epilepsy, mainly in children.[1] Popularly it is used for weight loss, and some in looksmaxxing communities also use it for leaning out and for acne claims.","For weight loss, Wikipedia reports that low-carbohydrate diets produce somewhat more short-term loss than low-fat diets, with the advantage fading over time, and a 2022 Cochrane review found no benefit over balanced diets at two years.[2] Acne effects are not covered in the sources consulted."],"infobox":[["Type","Diet"],["Original use","Refractory epilepsy"],["Term coined","1921, Russell Wilder (Mayo Clinic)"],["Common side effects","Constipation, fatigue early on"]],"sections":[{"h":"History","paras":["The term ketogenic diet was coined in 1921 by Russell Wilder at the Mayo Clinic, and Mynie Peterman formulated the classic diet in the 1920s, reporting in 1925 that 60 percent of 37 children became seizure-free.[1] The diet declined after phenytoin arrived in 1938 and revived in the 1990s.[1] Earlier low-carbohydrate regimens include William Banting's 1863 letter and Robert Atkins's 1972 book.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Weight loss","paras":["Short- and medium-term studies show somewhat more loss than low-fat diets, around 100 kcal a day, fading over time, and calorie intake and adherence largely determine long-term results.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Adverse effects","paras":["Reported effects include constipation, low-grade acidosis, raised blood lipids, and early lethargy that usually resolves within two weeks.[1] Low-carbohydrate diets have been associated in case reports with ketoacidosis, and common effects include headache, bad breath and cramps.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["Trials in epilepsy found seizures reduced by more than 50 percent in about half of patients.[1] Trials of low-carbohydrate diets for weight loss are summarized above.[2] No studies found on ketogenic diets for acne in the sources consulted."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1921","event":"Wilder coins the term ketogenic diet.[1]"},{"year":"1925","event":"Peterman reports seizure freedom in 60% of 37 children.[1]"},{"year":"1972","event":"Atkins publishes Dr. Atkins' Diet Revolution.[2]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Ketogenic diet","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ketogenic_diet","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Low-carbohydrate diet","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Low-carbohydrate_diet","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[{"title":"Ketogenic diet","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ketogenic_diet","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"kind":null},{"title":"Low-carbohydrate diet","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Low-carbohydrate_diet","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"kind":null}],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"keto diet - tough shit","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/keto-diet-tough-shit.15600/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250710165452/https://looksmax.org/threads/keto-diet-tough-shit.15600/"},{"title":"Redpill Keto/Raw meat diets are the healthiest.","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/keto-raw-meat-diets-are-the-healthiest.139/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20220524120544/https://looksmax.org/threads/keto-raw-meat-diets-are-the-healthiest.139/"},{"title":"Disastrous findings from Keto/Low Carb/High fat diet CTA study","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/disastrous-findings-from-keto-low-carb-high-fat-diet-cta-study.1408407/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250623064435/https://looksmax.org/threads/disastrous-findings-from-keto-low-carb-high-fat-diet-cta-study.1408407/"},{"title":"low carb keto dieting is totally overrated and stupid","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/low-carb-keto-dieting-is-totally-overrated-and-stupid.1400802/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20250623060923/https://looksmax.org/threads/low-carb-keto-dieting-is-totally-overrated-and-stupid.1400802/"},{"title":"does a keto diet ruin your kidneys or is that gaslighting","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/does-a-keto-diet-ruin-your-kidneys-or-is-that-gaslighting.1082139/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.archive.org/web/20240714100609/https://looksmax.org/threads/does-a-keto-diet-ruin-your-kidneys-or-is-that-gaslighting.1082139/"},{"title":"rate me after a gym session do i look leaner while on keto diet","url":"https://looksmax.org/threads/rate-me-after-a-gym-session-do-i-look-leaner-while-on-keto-diet.1034808/","site":"looksmax.org","archived":"https://web.ar